{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HdrG7oTxJ7mcJy54J83riA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Expense Policy — Fictional Meridian Works (MW)\n2\tFixture version: 1.0. All rules in this repository are fictional. The text is authoritative for the exercise.\n3\t\n4\t## EXP-1 Ordinary purchases\n5\tFor a routine non-travel purchase of $2,500 or less incurred on or after July 1, 2025, **manager approval** is required before purchase.\n6\t\n7\t## EXP-2 Higher-value purchases\n8\tFor a routine non-travel purchase above $2,500 incurred on or after July 1, 2025, **both manager and finance approval** are required before purchase.\n9\t\n10\t## EXP-3 Relationship to special policies\n11\tThe Emergency Policy may waive **advance finance approval**, but not manager approval. Vendor restrictions always apply. Airfare purchases are subject to the Travel Policy as well as the relevant purchase approval threshold in this Expense Policy. Relevant historical thresholds appear in the Amendments Policy.\n12\t\n13\t## EXP-4 Amounts\n14\tAll thresholds use the total transaction amount in US dollars, inclusive of taxes and fees. The phrases 'up to' and 'or less' are inclusive.\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76c568a8-58fd-487f-9fc8-df5240d0792d","uuid":"cc8b84b2-f1ca-470a-af7e-7ced27ad5178","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:45:17.083Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mmazu\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\cp14-seven-sessions-20261013\\C_SEVEN_01\\Q8\\01-expense-policy.md","content":"# Expense Policy — Fictional Meridian Works (MW)\nFixture version: 1.0. All rules in this repository are fictional. The text is authoritative for the exercise.\n\n## EXP-1 Ordinary purchases\nFor a routine non-travel purchase of $2,500 or less incurred on or after July 1, 2025, **manager approval** is required before purchase.\n\n## EXP-2 Higher-value purchases\nFor a routine non-travel purchase above $2,500 incurred on or after July 1, 2025, **both manager and finance approval** are required before purchase.\n\n## EXP-3 Relationship to special policies\nThe Emergency Policy may waive **advance finance approval**, but not manager approval. Vendor restrictions always apply. Airfare purchases are subject to the Travel Policy as well as the relevant purchase approval threshold in this Expense Policy. Relevant historical thresholds appear in the Amendments Policy.\n\n## EXP-4 Amounts\nAll thresholds use the total transaction amount in US dollars, inclusive of taxes and fees. The phrases 'up to' and 'or less' are inclusive.\n","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":15}}}
